  --------------------------------------------------------------
  ==> BOTTLENECK: CODEC/MDL: recombination is not rewarded (dL_compose <= 0)
  root cause: a CALL (opcode + gamma index) costs ~ the 2-3 literals it
  abstracts, and a module macro inflates every later macro index, so
  composing modules only pays beyond k~14 reuse -- and REP
  already captures repeated structure more cheaply (True).
  prescription: recombination needs a CODEC change (cheaper composition,
  e.g. a 2-macro COMPOSE opcode or smaller index cost), NOT more search or
  a bigger world.  Forcing it via mutation would not be self-organised.
